## Why This Is Asked

Tests real-time multi-tenant deployment, latency budgets, privacy guarantees, and drift monitoring in production-like settings.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time multi-tenant inference
- Early-exit and mixed-precision optimization
- DP/FL privacy guarantees and secure aggregation
- Drift detection and rollout strategy

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-inference skeleton for two-tower model
function twoTowerInfer(input, tenantId, model) {
  // shared backbone
  const shared = model.backbone.extract(input.features)
  // tenant-specific embedding
  const emb = model.tenantEmbeddings[tenantId](input.userId)
  // combine and head with early exit
  const fused = concatenate(shared, emb)
  return model.heads[0](fused) // early exit path
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to handle new tenants with cold-start data? 
- How to quantify privacy-utility trade-offs with DP/Secure Aggregation?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical lightweight baseline building for text routing under strict latency constraints, in a data-scarce regime with model calibration requirements. Also covers drift monitoring and retraining cadence.

## Key Concepts
- Lightweight text representation with a fixed 30-feature vector
- SGD-based multiclass logistic regression or tiny decision tree for efficiency
- Calibration via temperature scaling
- Drift detection using rolling holdout validation
- Deployment latency and monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Training loop outline for SGD multiclass LR
const model = new SGDLogisticRegression({
  learningRate: 0.01,
  epochs: 100,
  batchSize: 32
});
model.fit(XTrain, yTrain);
// Temperature scaling for calibration
const temp = calibrateTemperature(model, XVal, yVal);
// Inference
const predict = (features) => {
  const start = performance.now();
  const probs = model.predictProb(features, temp);
  const latency = performance.now() - start;
  return { probs, latency };
};
```

